  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper evaluates three quantum machine learning models for credit card fraud detection using the European 2013 dataset (284,807 transactions). QSVC with a ZZ feature map achieved the best reported performance with accuracy 0.9459, precision 1.00, and recall 0.87, outperforming the Pauli-feature QSVC (accuracy 0.9189) and a VQC classifier (accuracy 0.8514). Experiments were implemented in Qiskit in a simulated quantum environment with no reported circuit resources or hardware execution.",
